/-!
# Borel structure on a restricted product

Every restricted product `Πʳ i, [R i, A i]_[𝓕]` of topological spaces carries its Borel
`MeasurableSpace` (`RestrictedProduct.measurableSpace := borel _`) and `BorelSpace` instance
(`RestrictedProduct.borelSpace`). Coordinate evaluation, coercion to the full product, filter
inclusions, and single-factor insertions are measurable.

Over a countable index type `ι` (or a countable constrained set `S`):
* Any coordinate box `RestrictedProduct.box C` with Borel-measurable factors `C i` is measurable in
  `Πʳ i, [R i, A i]_[𝓕]` with no openness or cofinite-equality hypothesis (`measurableSet_box`);
  principal-stage inclusions (`𝓕 ≤ 𝓟 S`) are measurable embeddings whenever `S` is countable and
  the constrained reference sets `A i` are measurable, and `structureMap` is a measurable embedding
  when `ι` is countable, every `A i` is measurable, and `Π i, A i` is a `BorelSpace`.
* Whenever `ι` is countable and the full product `Π i, R i` is a `BorelSpace`, even though the
  coercion `(↑) : Πʳ i, [R i, A i] → Π i, R i` is in general not a topological embedding
  (`TauCeti.not_isInducing_coe_bot`), the Borel σ-algebra of `Πʳ i, [R i, A i]` unconditionally
  equals the pullback of the product σ-algebra (`comap_coe_eq_measurableSpace`) and is generated by
  the π-system `measurableBoxes R A` (`measurableSpace_eq_generateFrom_measurableBoxes`), with no
  openness or measurability assumption on `A i`; measurability of maps into `Πʳ i, [R i, A i]` is
  therefore detected coordinatewise (`measurable_rng_iff`).
* When `A i` is measurable for cofinitely many `i`, the smaller π-system
  `cofiniteMeasurableBoxes R A` also generates the Borel σ-algebra
  (`measurableSpace_eq_generateFrom_cofiniteMeasurableBoxes`) and `(↑)` is a `MeasurableEmbedding`
  (`measurableEmbedding_coe`). When each `R i` is second countable and `A i` is open for cofinitely
  many `i`, `cofiniteOpenBoxes R A` generates the Borel σ-algebra
  (`measurableSpace_eq_generateFrom_cofiniteOpenBoxes`).

## Main definitions and results

* `RestrictedProduct.measurableSpace`, `RestrictedProduct.borelSpace`: Borel `MeasurableSpace` and
  `BorelSpace` instances on `Πʳ i, [R i, A i]_[𝓕]`.
* `RestrictedProduct.measurable_eval`, `RestrictedProduct.measurable_coe`,
  `RestrictedProduct.measurable_inclusion`, `RestrictedProduct.measurable_structureMap`,
  `RestrictedProduct.measurable_mulSingle`: measurability of structural maps.
* `RestrictedProduct.measurableEmbedding_inclusion_principal`,
  `RestrictedProduct.measurableEmbedding_structureMap`: measurable embeddings of principal stages
  (for countable `S` with measurable constrained `A i`) and of `structureMap` (under
  `[BorelSpace (Π i, A i)]` and measurable `A i`).
* `RestrictedProduct.measurableSet_box`: countable intersections make every Borel box measurable.
* `RestrictedProduct.measurableSet_box_of_eventually_eq`: over an arbitrary index type, a Borel box
  agreeing cofinitely with cofinitely open reference sets is measurable.
* `RestrictedProduct.measurableSpace_eq_generateFrom_cofiniteOpenBoxes`,
  `RestrictedProduct.measurableSpace_eq_generateFrom_cofiniteMeasurableBoxes`,
  `RestrictedProduct.measurableSpace_eq_generateFrom_measurableBoxes`: generation of the Borel
  σ-algebra by box π-systems.
* `RestrictedProduct.comap_coe_eq_measurableSpace_of_principal`,
  `RestrictedProduct.measurable_rng_iff_of_principal`,
  `RestrictedProduct.comap_coe_eq_measurableSpace`, `RestrictedProduct.measurable_rng_iff`,
  `RestrictedProduct.measurableEmbedding_coe`: comparison with the product σ-algebra on `Π i, R i`.
* `TauCeti.measurableSet_integralSubgroupOf_of_isOpen_of_eventually_le`,
  `TauCeti.measurableSet_integralSubgroupOf`, `TauCeti.measurableSet_integralSubgroup`:
  measurability of integral and level subgroups.
* `TauCeti.measurable_restrictedProductSplit`, `TauCeti.measurable_restrictedProductSplit_symm`,
  `TauCeti.restrictedProductSplitMeasurableEquiv`: the splitting of a restricted product at a
  finite set of indices is a measurable equivalence.

## References

* N. Bourbaki, *General Topology*.
* D. Bump, *Automorphic Forms and Representations*, §3.1.
* D. Ramakrishnan and R. J. Valenza, *Fourier Analysis on Number Fields*, Chapter 5.
* J. Tate, *Fourier analysis in number fields and Hecke's zeta-functions*, §3.3.
* A. Weil, *Basic Number Theory*.
-/

public section

open Filter MeasureTheory Set Topology
open scoped RestrictedProduct

namespace RestrictedProduct

section Basic

variable {ι : Type*} {R : ι → Type*} {A : ∀ i, Set (R i)} {𝓕 : Filter ι}
variable [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (R i)]

variable (R A 𝓕) in
/-- Every restricted product of topological spaces carries its Borel σ-algebra. -/
instance measurableSpace : MeasurableSpace (Πʳ i, [R i, A i]_[𝓕]) :=
  borel _

/-- Every restricted product of topological spaces is a `BorelSpace` for its canonical
`MeasurableSpace`. -/
instance borelSpace : BorelSpace (Πʳ i, [R i, A i]_[𝓕]) :=
  ⟨rfl⟩

/-- Coordinate evaluation at `i` on `Πʳ j, [R j, A j]_[𝓕]` is measurable whenever `R i` is a
Borel space. -/
@[fun_prop]
theorem measurable_eval (i : ι) [MeasurableSpace (R i)] [BorelSpace (R i)] :
    Measurable (fun x : Πʳ j, [R j, A j]_[𝓕] ↦ x i) :=
  (continuous_eval i).measurable

/-- Coercion from `Πʳ i, [R i, A i]_[𝓕]` to the full product `Π i, R i` is measurable for the
product σ-algebra whenever every factor `R i` is a Borel space. -/
@[fun_prop]
theorem measurable_coe [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] [∀ i, BorelSpace (R i)] :
    Measurable ((↑) : Πʳ i, [R i, A i]_[𝓕] → Π i, R i) :=
  measurable_pi_iff.mpr fun i ↦ measurable_eval i

/-- Filter inclusion `Πʳ i, [R i, A i]_[𝓖] → Πʳ i, [R i, A i]_[𝓕]` (`𝓕 ≤ 𝓖`) is measurable. -/
@[fun_prop]
theorem measurable_inclusion {𝓖 : Filter ι} (h : 𝓕 ≤ 𝓖) :
    Measurable (inclusion R A h) :=
  (continuous_inclusion h).measurable

/-- When the product `Π i, A i` has measurable open sets, `structureMap R A 𝓕` into
`Πʳ i, [R i, A i]_[𝓕]` is measurable. -/
@[fun_prop]
theorem measurable_structureMap [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] [OpensMeasurableSpace (Π i, A i)] :
    Measurable (structureMap R A 𝓕) :=
  isEmbedding_structureMap.continuous.measurable

/-- On a principal stage `Πʳ i, [R i, A i]_[𝓟 S]`, whenever the full product `Π i, R i` is a
`BorelSpace`, the Borel σ-algebra is the pullback of the product σ-algebra. -/
theorem comap_coe_eq_measurableSpace_of_principal [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)]
    [BorelSpace (Π i, R i)] {S : Set ι} :
    MeasurableSpace.pi.comap ((↑) : Πʳ i, [R i, A i]_[𝓟 S] → Π i, R i) =
      measurableSpace R A (𝓟 S) := by
  rw [BorelSpace.measurable_eq (α := Π i, R i), isEmbedding_coe_of_principal.isInducing.comap_borel]
  rfl

/-- Whenever the full product `Π i, R i` is a `BorelSpace`, a map into a principal stage
`Πʳ i, [R i, A i]_[𝓟 S]` is measurable if and only if all of its coordinate maps are measurable. -/
theorem measurable_rng_iff_of_principal [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)]
    [BorelSpace (Π i, R i)] {S : Set ι} {X : Type*}
    [MeasurableSpace X] {f : X → Πʳ i, [R i, A i]_[𝓟 S]} :
    Measurable f ↔ ∀ i, Measurable (fun x ↦ f x i) := by
  rw [← isEmbedding_coe_of_principal.isInducing.measurable_comp_iff, measurable_pi_iff]
  rfl

end Basic

section MulSingle

variable {ι : Type*} [DecidableEq ι] {G : ι → Type*} {S : ι → Type*}
variable [∀ i, SetLike (S i) (G i)] [∀ i, One (G i)] [∀ i, OneMemClass (S i) (G i)]
variable [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (G i)]

/-- Inserting a single factor at `i` into `Πʳ j, [G j, B j]` is measurable whenever `G i` has
measurable open sets. -/
@[to_additive (attr := fun_prop)
  /-- Inserting a single additive factor at `i` into `Πʳ j, [G j, B j]` is measurable whenever
  `G i` has measurable open sets. -/]
theorem measurable_mulSingle (B : ∀ i, S i) (i : ι) [MeasurableSpace (G i)]
    [OpensMeasurableSpace (G i)] :
    Measurable (mulSingle B i) :=
  (TauCeti.continuous_restrictedProduct_mulSingle B i).measurable

end MulSingle

section Boxes

variable {ι : Type*} {R : ι → Type*} {A : ∀ i, Set (R i)}

/-- Over a countable index type, a coordinate box `box C` with measurable factors `C i` in Borel
spaces `R i` is measurable in `Πʳ i, [R i, A i]_[𝓕]` for every filter `𝓕` and arbitrary reference
sets `A i`. -/
theorem measurableSet_box [Countable ι] [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (R i)]
    [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] [∀ i, BorelSpace (R i)] {𝓕 : Filter ι} {C : ∀ i, Set (R i)}
    (hC : ∀ i, MeasurableSet (C i)) :
    MeasurableSet (box C : Set (Πʳ i, [R i, A i]_[𝓕])) := by
  rw [box_eq_iInter]
  exact MeasurableSet.iInter fun i ↦ (hC i).preimage (measurable_eval i)

/-- Over an arbitrary (possibly uncountable) index type, a coordinate box `box C` with measurable
factors `C i` in Borel spaces `R i` is measurable in `Πʳ i, [R i, A i]` whenever cofinitely many
`A i` are open and `C i = A i` cofinitely: it is an open box cut down by finitely many coordinate
conditions. -/
theorem measurableSet_box_of_eventually_eq [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (R i)]
    [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] [∀ i, BorelSpace (R i)] {C : ∀ i, Set (R i)}
    (hA : ∀ᶠ i in cofinite, IsOpen (A i)) (hC : ∀ i, MeasurableSet (C i))
    (hCA : ∀ᶠ i in cofinite, C i = A i) :
    MeasurableSet (box C : Set (Πʳ i, [R i, A i])) := by
  classical
  have hF := mem_cofinite.mp (hA.and hCA)
  let F : Finset ι := hF.toFinset
  have hnotF (i : ι) (hi : i ∉ F) : IsOpen (A i) ∧ C i = A i :=
    Classical.byContradiction fun h ↦ hi (hF.mem_toFinset.mpr h)
  let D : ∀ i, Set (R i) := fun i ↦ if i ∈ F then univ else C i
  have hD : IsOpen (box D : Set (Πʳ i, [R i, A i])) := by
    refine isOpen_box_of_eventually_eq (fun i ↦ ?_) ?_
    · by_cases hi : i ∈ F
      · simp [D, hi]
      · simpa [D, hi, (hnotF i hi).2] using (hnotF i hi).1
    · filter_upwards [F.finite_toSet.compl_mem_cofinite] with i hi
      have hi' : i ∉ F := hi
      simp [D, hi', (hnotF i hi').2]
  have heq : (box C : Set (Πʳ i, [R i, A i])) = box D ∩ ⋂ i ∈ F, (fun x ↦ x i) ⁻¹' C i := by
    ext x
    simp only [mem_box, mem_inter_iff, mem_iInter, mem_preimage]
    refine ⟨fun hx ↦ ⟨fun i ↦ ?_, fun i _ ↦ hx i⟩, fun ⟨hxD, hxF⟩ i ↦ ?_⟩
    · by_cases hi : i ∈ F <;> simp [D, hi, hx i]
    · by_cases hi : i ∈ F
      · exact hxF i hi
      · simpa [D, hi] using hxD i
  rw [heq]
  exact hD.measurableSet.inter
    (Finset.measurableSet_biInter F fun i _ ↦ (hC i).preimage (measurable_eval i))

/-- With Borel factors, the range of `inclusion R A hS` for a principal filter `𝓟 S` (`𝓕 ≤ 𝓟 S`)
is measurable whenever `S` is countable and `A i` is measurable for every `i ∈ S`. -/
theorem measurableSet_range_inclusion_principal [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (R i)]
    [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] [∀ i, BorelSpace (R i)] {𝓕 : Filter ι} {S : Set ι}
    (hS : 𝓕 ≤ 𝓟 S) (hSc : S.Countable) (hA : ∀ i ∈ S, MeasurableSet (A i)) :
    MeasurableSet (range (inclusion R A hS)) := by
  have hrange : range (inclusion R A hS) =
      ((↑) : Πʳ i, [R i, A i]_[𝓕] → Π i, R i) ⁻¹' S.pi A := by
    ext x
    rw [range_inclusion, mem_ofPred_eq, eventually_principal, mem_preimage, Set.mem_pi]
  rw [hrange]
  exact (MeasurableSet.pi hSc hA).preimage measurable_coe

/-- Over a countable index type with Borel factors, the range of `structureMap R A 𝓕` (the integral
box `box A`) is measurable whenever every `A i` is measurable. -/
theorem measurableSet_range_structureMap [Countable ι] [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (R i)]
    [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] [∀ i, BorelSpace (R i)] {𝓕 : Filter ι}
    (hA : ∀ i, MeasurableSet (A i)) :
    MeasurableSet (range (structureMap R A 𝓕)) := by
  convert measurableSet_box (R := R) (A := A) (𝓕 := 𝓕) hA using 1
  -- `range_structureMap` uses `f.1 i`, defeq to `f i` via `RestrictedProduct`'s `DFunLike`.
  rw [range_structureMap, box_def]
  rfl

/-- With Borel factors, the inclusion of a principal stage `Πʳ i, [R i, A i]_[𝓟 S]` into
`Πʳ i, [R i, A i]_[𝓕]` (`𝓕 ≤ 𝓟 S`) is a measurable embedding whenever `S` is countable and `A i`
is measurable for every `i ∈ S`. -/
theorem measurableEmbedding_inclusion_principal [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (R i)]
    [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] [∀ i, BorelSpace (R i)] {𝓕 : Filter ι} {S : Set ι}
    (hS : 𝓕 ≤ 𝓟 S) (hSc : S.Countable) (hA : ∀ i ∈ S, MeasurableSet (A i)) :
    MeasurableEmbedding (inclusion R A hS) :=
  (isEmbedding_inclusion_principal hS).measurableEmbedding
    (measurableSet_range_inclusion_principal hS hSc hA)

/-- Over a countable index type with Borel factors and a Borel product `Π i, A i`,
`structureMap R A 𝓕 : (Π i, A i) → Πʳ i, [R i, A i]_[𝓕]` is a measurable embedding whenever every
`A i` is measurable in `R i`. -/
theorem measurableEmbedding_structureMap [Countable ι] [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (R i)]
    [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] [∀ i, BorelSpace (R i)] [BorelSpace (Π i, A i)]
    {𝓕 : Filter ι} (hA : ∀ i, MeasurableSet (A i)) :
    MeasurableEmbedding (structureMap R A 𝓕) :=
  isEmbedding_structureMap.measurableEmbedding (measurableSet_range_structureMap hA)

/-- `cofiniteOpenBoxes R A` is a π-system on `Πʳ i, [R i, A i]`. -/
theorem isPiSystem_cofiniteOpenBoxes [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (R i)] :
    IsPiSystem (cofiniteOpenBoxes R A) :=
  fun _ hs _ ht _ ↦ inter_mem_cofiniteOpenBoxes hs ht

variable (R A) in
/-- Coordinate boxes `box C` in `Πʳ i, [R i, A i]` with measurable factors `C i` satisfying
`C i = A i` for cofinitely many `i`. -/
def cofiniteMeasurableBoxes [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] : Set (Set (Πʳ i, [R i, A i])) :=
  {s | ∃ C : ∀ i, Set (R i),
    (∀ i, MeasurableSet (C i)) ∧ (∀ᶠ i in cofinite, C i = A i) ∧ s = box C}

variable (R A) in
/-- Unfolding `cofiniteMeasurableBoxes R A` as the set of coordinate boxes with measurable factors
cofinitely equal to `A i`. -/
theorem cofiniteMeasurableBoxes_def [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] :
    cofiniteMeasurableBoxes R A =
      {s | ∃ C : ∀ i, Set (R i),
        (∀ i, MeasurableSet (C i)) ∧ (∀ᶠ i in cofinite, C i = A i) ∧ s = box C} :=
  (rfl)

/-- Membership in `cofiniteMeasurableBoxes R A`. -/
@[simp, grind =]
theorem mem_cofiniteMeasurableBoxes_iff [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)]
    {s : Set (Πʳ i, [R i, A i])} :
    s ∈ cofiniteMeasurableBoxes R A ↔
      ∃ C : ∀ i, Set (R i),
        (∀ i, MeasurableSet (C i)) ∧ (∀ᶠ i in cofinite, C i = A i) ∧ s = box C :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- A coordinate box `box C` with measurable factors cofinitely equal to `A i` belongs to
`cofiniteMeasurableBoxes R A`. -/
theorem box_mem_cofiniteMeasurableBoxes [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] {C : ∀ i, Set (R i)}
    (hC : ∀ i, MeasurableSet (C i)) (hCA : ∀ᶠ i in cofinite, C i = A i) :
    (box C : Set (Πʳ i, [R i, A i])) ∈ cofiniteMeasurableBoxes R A :=
  ⟨C, hC, hCA, rfl⟩

/-- Over a countable index type with Borel factors, every set in `cofiniteMeasurableBoxes R A` is
measurable in `Πʳ i, [R i, A i]`. -/
theorem measurableSet_of_mem_cofiniteMeasurableBoxes [Countable ι] [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (R i)]
    [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] [∀ i, BorelSpace (R i)] {s : Set (Πʳ i, [R i, A i])}
    (hs : s ∈ cofiniteMeasurableBoxes R A) :
    MeasurableSet s := by
  rcases hs with ⟨C, hC, -, rfl⟩
  exact measurableSet_box hC

/-- `cofiniteMeasurableBoxes R A` is a π-system on `Πʳ i, [R i, A i]`. -/
theorem isPiSystem_cofiniteMeasurableBoxes [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] :
    IsPiSystem (cofiniteMeasurableBoxes R A) := by
  rintro _ ⟨C, hC, hCA, rfl⟩ _ ⟨D, hD, hDA, rfl⟩ _
  refine ⟨fun i ↦ C i ∩ D i, fun i ↦ (hC i).inter (hD i), ?_, (box_inter C D).symm⟩
  exact (hCA.and hDA).mono fun i ⟨hiC, hiD⟩ ↦ by simp [hiC, hiD]

variable (R A) in
/-- All coordinate boxes `box C` in `Πʳ i, [R i, A i]` with measurable factors `C i`. -/
def measurableBoxes [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] : Set (Set (Πʳ i, [R i, A i])) :=
  {s | ∃ C : ∀ i, Set (R i), (∀ i, MeasurableSet (C i)) ∧ s = box C}

variable (R A) in
/-- Unfolding `measurableBoxes R A` as the set of coordinate boxes with measurable factors. -/
theorem measurableBoxes_def [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] :
    measurableBoxes R A = {s | ∃ C : ∀ i, Set (R i), (∀ i, MeasurableSet (C i)) ∧ s = box C} :=
  (rfl)

/-- Membership in `measurableBoxes R A`. -/
@[simp, grind =]
theorem mem_measurableBoxes_iff [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] {s : Set (Πʳ i, [R i, A i])} :
    s ∈ measurableBoxes R A ↔ ∃ C : ∀ i, Set (R i), (∀ i, MeasurableSet (C i)) ∧ s = box C :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- A coordinate box `box C` with measurable factors belongs to `measurableBoxes R A`. -/
theorem box_mem_measurableBoxes [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] {C : ∀ i, Set (R i)}
    (hC : ∀ i, MeasurableSet (C i)) :
    (box C : Set (Πʳ i, [R i, A i])) ∈ measurableBoxes R A :=
  ⟨C, hC, rfl⟩

/-- Over a countable index type with Borel factors, every set in `measurableBoxes R A` is
measurable in `Πʳ i, [R i, A i]`. -/
theorem measurableSet_of_mem_measurableBoxes [Countable ι] [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (R i)]
    [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] [∀ i, BorelSpace (R i)] {s : Set (Πʳ i, [R i, A i])}
    (hs : s ∈ measurableBoxes R A) :
    MeasurableSet s := by
  rcases hs with ⟨C, hC, rfl⟩
  exact measurableSet_box hC

/-- `measurableBoxes R A` is a π-system on `Πʳ i, [R i, A i]`. -/
theorem isPiSystem_measurableBoxes [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] :
    IsPiSystem (measurableBoxes R A) := by
  rintro _ ⟨C, hC, rfl⟩ _ ⟨D, hD, rfl⟩ _
  exact ⟨fun i ↦ C i ∩ D i, fun i ↦ (hC i).inter (hD i), (box_inter C D).symm⟩

/-- Every open cofinitely-`A i` box is a cofinitely-`A i` measurable box when open sets are
measurable in each factor. -/
theorem cofiniteOpenBoxes_subset_cofiniteMeasurableBoxes [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (R i)]
    [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] [∀ i, OpensMeasurableSpace (R i)] :
    cofiniteOpenBoxes R A ⊆ cofiniteMeasurableBoxes R A := by
  intro _ hs
  obtain ⟨C, hC, hCA, rfl⟩ := mem_cofiniteOpenBoxes_iff.mp hs
  exact box_mem_cofiniteMeasurableBoxes (fun i ↦ (hC i).measurableSet) hCA

/-- Every cofinitely-`A i` measurable box belongs to `measurableBoxes R A`. -/
theorem cofiniteMeasurableBoxes_subset_measurableBoxes [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] :
    cofiniteMeasurableBoxes R A ⊆ measurableBoxes R A := by
  rintro _ ⟨C, hC, -, rfl⟩
  exact box_mem_measurableBoxes hC

/-- Over a countable index type with second-countable factors and `A i` cofinitely open, the Borel
σ-algebra of `Πʳ i, [R i, A i]` is generated by `cofiniteOpenBoxes R A`. -/
theorem measurableSpace_eq_generateFrom_cofiniteOpenBoxes [Countable ι]
    [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (R i)] [∀ i, SecondCountableTopology (R i)]
    (hA : ∀ᶠ i in cofinite, IsOpen (A i)) :
    measurableSpace R A cofinite = MeasurableSpace.generateFrom (cofiniteOpenBoxes R A) := by
  have := secondCountableTopology_of_cofinite (R := R) hA
  exact (isTopologicalBasis_cofiniteOpenBoxes hA).borel_eq_generateFrom

/-- Over a countable index type with a Borel product `Π i, R i`, the Borel σ-algebra of
`Πʳ i, [R i, A i]` equals the pullback of the product σ-algebra along the coercion
`(↑) : Πʳ i, [R i, A i] → Π i, R i`, with no openness or measurability assumption on `A i`. -/
theorem comap_coe_eq_measurableSpace [Countable ι] [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (R i)]
    [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] [BorelSpace (Π i, R i)] :
    MeasurableSpace.pi.comap ((↑) : Πʳ i, [R i, A i] → Π i, R i) =
      measurableSpace R A cofinite := by
  apply le_antisymm continuous_coe.measurable.comap_le
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := exists_injective_nat ι
  let S : ℕ → Set ι := fun n ↦ {i | n ≤ e i}
  have hS : ∀ n : ℕ, cofinite ≤ 𝓟 (S n) := fun n ↦ le_principal_iff.mpr <| mem_cofinite.mpr <|
    ((Finset.range n).finite_toSet.preimage he.injOn).subset fun i hi ↦ by
      simp only [S, mem_compl_iff, mem_ofPred_eq, not_le] at hi
      simpa using hi
  refine MeasurableSpace.generateFrom_le fun U hU ↦ ?_
  have hex : ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ W : Set (Π i, R i), MeasurableSet W ∧
      ((↑) : Πʳ i, [R i, A i]_[𝓟 (S n)] → Π i, R i) ⁻¹' W = inclusion R A (hS n) ⁻¹' U := by
    intro n
    rw [← MeasurableSpace.measurableSet_comap, comap_coe_eq_measurableSpace_of_principal]
    exact (hU.preimage (continuous_inclusion (hS n))).measurableSet
  choose W hWm hW using hex
  refine ⟨⋂ m : ℕ, ⋃ (n : ℕ) (_ : m ≤ n), W n,
    MeasurableSet.iInter fun m ↦ MeasurableSet.iUnion fun n ↦
      MeasurableSet.iUnion fun _ ↦ hWm n, ?_⟩
  ext x
  have hfin : (e '' {i | x i ∉ A i}).Finite := (mem_cofinite.mp x.property).image e
  let m₀ : ℕ := hfin.toFinset.sup id + 1
  have hm₀ : ∀ n ≥ m₀, (x : Π i, R i) ∈ W n ↔ x ∈ U := fun n hn ↦ by
    have hxS : ∀ᶠ i in 𝓟 (S n), x i ∈ A i := eventually_principal.mpr fun i hi ↦ by
      by_contra hxA
      have hle : e i ≤ hfin.toFinset.sup id :=
        Finset.le_sup (f := id) (hfin.mem_toFinset.mpr ⟨i, hxA, rfl⟩)
      have hni : n ≤ e i := hi
      omega
    obtain ⟨x', hx'⟩ := exists_inclusion_eq_of_eventually R A (hS n) hxS
    have hcoe : (x' : Π i, R i) = (x : Π i, R i) := funext fun i ↦ by rw [← hx', inclusion_apply]
    rw [← hcoe, ← mem_preimage, hW n, mem_preimage, hx']
  simp only [mem_preimage, mem_iInter, mem_iUnion, exists_prop]
  exact ⟨fun h ↦ (hm₀ _ (h m₀).choose_spec.1).mp (h m₀).choose_spec.2,
    fun hxU m ↦ ⟨max m m₀, le_max_left _ _, (hm₀ _ (le_max_right _ _)).mpr hxU⟩⟩

/-- Over a countable index type with a Borel product `Π i, R i`, a map `f` into
`Πʳ i, [R i, A i]` is measurable if and only if each coordinate `x ↦ f x i` is measurable, with no
openness or measurability assumption on `A i`. -/
theorem measurable_rng_iff [Countable ι] [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (R i)]
    [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] [BorelSpace (Π i, R i)]
    {X : Type*} [MeasurableSpace X] {f : X → Πʳ i, [R i, A i]} :
    Measurable f ↔ ∀ i, Measurable (fun x ↦ f x i) := by
  rw [measurable_iff_comap_le, ← comap_coe_eq_measurableSpace, MeasurableSpace.comap_comp,
    ← measurable_iff_comap_le, measurable_pi_iff]
  rfl

/-- Over a countable index type with a Borel product `Π i, R i`, the Borel σ-algebra of
`Πʳ i, [R i, A i]` is generated by `measurableBoxes R A`, with no openness or measurability
assumption on `A i`. -/
theorem measurableSpace_eq_generateFrom_measurableBoxes [Countable ι] [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (R i)]
    [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] [BorelSpace (Π i, R i)] :
    measurableSpace R A cofinite = MeasurableSpace.generateFrom (measurableBoxes R A) := by
  classical
  rw [← comap_coe_eq_measurableSpace]
  apply le_antisymm
  · rw [MeasurableSpace.pi, MeasurableSpace.comap_iSup]
    refine iSup_le fun i ↦ ?_
    rw [MeasurableSpace.comap_comp]
    rintro _ ⟨B, hB, rfl⟩
    rw [preimage_comp, ← Set.univ_pi_update_univ, preimage_coe_univ_pi]
    exact MeasurableSpace.measurableSet_generateFrom <| box_mem_measurableBoxes <|
      (Function.forall_update_iff _ fun j s ↦ MeasurableSet s).mpr
        ⟨hB, fun _ _ ↦ MeasurableSet.univ⟩
  · refine MeasurableSpace.generateFrom_le ?_
    rintro _ ⟨C, hC, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨univ.pi C, MeasurableSet.univ_pi hC, preimage_coe_univ_pi C⟩

private theorem measurableSet_ite_mem_union [DecidableEq ι] [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)]
    (hA : ∀ᶠ i in cofinite, MeasurableSet (A i)) (F : Finset ι) (i : ι) :
    MeasurableSet
      (if i ∈ (mem_cofinite.mp hA).toFinset ∪ F then (univ : Set (R i)) else A i) := by
  split_ifs with hi
  · exact MeasurableSet.univ
  · by_contra hnot
    exact hi (Finset.mem_union_left _ ((mem_cofinite.mp hA).mem_toFinset.mpr hnot))

/-- Over a countable index type with a Borel product `Π i, R i` and `A i` cofinitely measurable,
the Borel σ-algebra of `Πʳ i, [R i, A i]` is generated by `cofiniteMeasurableBoxes R A`. -/
theorem measurableSpace_eq_generateFrom_cofiniteMeasurableBoxes [Countable ι]
    [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (R i)] [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] [BorelSpace (Π i, R i)]
    (hA : ∀ᶠ i in cofinite, MeasurableSet (A i)) :
    measurableSpace R A cofinite = MeasurableSpace.generateFrom (cofiniteMeasurableBoxes R A) := by
  classical
  rw [← comap_coe_eq_measurableSpace]
  apply le_antisymm
  · rw [MeasurableSpace.pi, MeasurableSpace.comap_iSup]
    refine iSup_le fun i₀ ↦ ?_
    rw [MeasurableSpace.comap_comp]
    rintro _ ⟨B, hB, rfl⟩
    let S₀ : Finset ι := (mem_cofinite.mp hA).toFinset
    let C : Finset ι → ∀ i, Set (R i) := fun F i ↦ if i ∈ S₀ ∪ F then univ else A i
    have hpre : (Function.eval i₀ ∘ ((↑) : Πʳ i, [R i, A i] → Π i, R i)) ⁻¹' B =
        ⋃ F : Finset ι, box (Function.update (C F) i₀ B) := by
      ext x
      simp only [mem_preimage, Function.comp_apply, Function.eval, mem_iUnion, mem_box]
      refine ⟨fun hx ↦ ⟨(mem_cofinite.mp x.property).toFinset, fun i ↦ ?_⟩, fun ⟨F, hF⟩ ↦ ?_⟩
      · rcases eq_or_ne i i₀ with rfl | hi₀
        · simpa using hx
        · rw [Function.update_of_ne hi₀]
          simp only [C]
          split_ifs with hi
          · exact mem_univ _
          · by_contra hnot
            exact hi (Finset.mem_union_right _ ((mem_cofinite.mp x.property).mem_toFinset.mpr hnot))
      · simpa using hF i₀
    rw [hpre]
    refine @MeasurableSet.iUnion _ _
      (MeasurableSpace.generateFrom (cofiniteMeasurableBoxes R A)) _ _ fun F ↦
      MeasurableSpace.measurableSet_generateFrom (box_mem_cofiniteMeasurableBoxes ?_ ?_)
    · intro i
      rcases eq_or_ne i i₀ with rfl | hi₀
      · simpa using hB
      · rw [Function.update_of_ne hi₀]
        exact measurableSet_ite_mem_union hA F i
    · filter_upwards [(insert i₀ (S₀ ∪ F)).finite_toSet.compl_mem_cofinite] with i hi
      simp_all [C]
  · refine MeasurableSpace.generateFrom_le ?_
    rintro _ ⟨C, hC, -, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨univ.pi C, MeasurableSet.univ_pi hC, preimage_coe_univ_pi C⟩

/-- Over a countable index type, the range of `(↑) : Πʳ i, [R i, A i] → Π i, R i` is measurable in
the product σ-algebra whenever `A i` is measurable for cofinitely many `i`. -/
theorem measurableSet_range_coe [Countable ι] [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)]
    (hA : ∀ᶠ i in cofinite, MeasurableSet (A i)) :
    MeasurableSet (range ((↑) : Πʳ i, [R i, A i] → Π i, R i)) := by
  classical
  rw [range_coe_eq_iUnion_univ_pi (mem_cofinite.mp hA).toFinset]
  exact MeasurableSet.iUnion fun F ↦ MeasurableSet.univ_pi (measurableSet_ite_mem_union hA F)

/-- Over a countable index type with a Borel product `Π i, R i`, `(↑) : Πʳ i, [R i, A i] →
Π i, R i` is a measurable embedding whenever `A i` is measurable for cofinitely many `i`. -/
theorem measurableEmbedding_coe [Countable ι] [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (R i)]
    [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] [BorelSpace (Π i, R i)]
    (hA : ∀ᶠ i in cofinite, MeasurableSet (A i)) :
    MeasurableEmbedding ((↑) : Πʳ i, [R i, A i] → Π i, R i) :=
  MeasurableEmbedding.iff_comap_eq.mpr
    ⟨DFunLike.coe_injective, comap_coe_eq_measurableSpace, measurableSet_range_coe hA⟩

end Boxes

end RestrictedProduct

namespace TauCeti

section IntegralSubgroups

variable {ι : Type*} {G : ι → Type*} [∀ i, Group (G i)]

/-- Any open level subgroup `integralSubgroupOf U V` (with `V i` open and `U i ≤ V i` cofinitely)
is Borel measurable in `Πʳ i, [G i, U i]`, with no countability assumption on `ι`. -/
@[to_additive
  /-- Any open level additive subgroup `integralAddSubgroupOf U V` (with `V i` open and
  `U i ≤ V i` cofinitely) is Borel measurable in `Πʳ i, [G i, U i]`, with no countability
  assumption on `ι`. -/]
theorem measurableSet_integralSubgroupOf_of_isOpen_of_eventually_le [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (G i)]
    (U V : ∀ i, Subgroup (G i)) (hV : ∀ i, IsOpen (V i : Set (G i)))
    (hUV : ∀ᶠ i in cofinite, U i ≤ V i) :
    MeasurableSet (integralSubgroupOf U V : Set (Πʳ i, [G i, (U i : Set (G i))])) :=
  (isOpen_integralSubgroupOf_of_eventually_le U V hV hUV).measurableSet

/-- Over a countable index type with Borel factors, `integralSubgroupOf U V` is measurable whenever
every `V i` is Borel measurable, with no openness or cofinite-inclusion hypothesis. -/
@[to_additive
  /-- Over a countable index type with Borel factors, `integralAddSubgroupOf U V` is measurable
  whenever every `V i` is Borel measurable, with no openness or cofinite-inclusion hypothesis. -/]
theorem measurableSet_integralSubgroupOf [Countable ι] [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (G i)]
    [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (G i)] [∀ i, BorelSpace (G i)] (U V : ∀ i, Subgroup (G i))
    (hV : ∀ i, MeasurableSet (V i : Set (G i))) :
    MeasurableSet (integralSubgroupOf U V : Set (Πʳ i, [G i, (U i : Set (G i))])) := by
  rw [coe_integralSubgroupOf_eq_box]
  exact RestrictedProduct.measurableSet_box hV

/-- Over a countable index type with Borel factors, `integralSubgroup U` is measurable whenever
every `U i` is Borel measurable. -/
@[to_additive
  /-- Over a countable index type with Borel factors, `integralAddSubgroup U` is measurable
  whenever every `U i` is Borel measurable. -/]
theorem measurableSet_integralSubgroup [Countable ι] [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (G i)]
    [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (G i)] [∀ i, BorelSpace (G i)] (U : ∀ i, Subgroup (G i))
    (hU : ∀ i, MeasurableSet (U i : Set (G i))) :
    MeasurableSet (integralSubgroup U : Set (Πʳ i, [G i, (U i : Set (G i))])) := by
  rw [← integralSubgroupOf_self]
  exact measurableSet_integralSubgroupOf U U hU

end IntegralSubgroups

section Split

open RestrictedProduct

variable {ι : Type*} [Countable ι] {G : ι → Type*} {K : ι → Type*}
  [∀ i, Group (G i)] [∀ i, SetLike (K i) (G i)] [∀ i, SubgroupClass (K i) (G i)]
  [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (G i)] [∀ i, SecondCountableTopology (G i)]
  [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (G i)] [∀ i, BorelSpace (G i)] (B : ∀ i, K i) (T : Finset ι)

/-- `restrictedProductSplit B T` is measurable. -/
@[to_additive (attr := fun_prop) measurable_addRestrictedProductSplit
/-- `addRestrictedProductSplit B T` is measurable. -/]
theorem measurable_restrictedProductSplit : Measurable (restrictedProductSplit B T) := by
  refine Measurable.prod (measurable_pi_iff.mpr fun i ↦ ?_) (measurable_rng_iff.mpr fun i ↦ ?_)
  · simp_rw [restrictedProductSplit_apply_fst]
    exact measurable_eval i.val
  · simp_rw [restrictedProductSplit_apply_snd]
    exact measurable_eval (R := G) i.val

/-- The inverse of `restrictedProductSplit B T` is measurable. -/
@[to_additive (attr := fun_prop) measurable_addRestrictedProductSplit_symm
/-- The inverse of `addRestrictedProductSplit B T` is measurable. -/]
theorem measurable_restrictedProductSplit_symm :
    Measurable (restrictedProductSplit B T).symm := by
  refine measurable_rng_iff.mpr fun i ↦ ?_
  by_cases hi : i ∈ T
  · simp_rw [restrictedProductSplit_symm_apply_of_mem B T _ hi]
    exact (measurable_pi_apply _).comp measurable_fst
  · simp_rw [restrictedProductSplit_symm_apply_of_notMem B T _ hi]
    exact (measurable_eval (R := fun i : {i // i ∉ T} ↦ G i.val) ⟨i, hi⟩).comp measurable_snd

/-- `restrictedProductSplit B T` as a measurable equivalence. -/
@[to_additive addRestrictedProductSplitMeasurableEquiv
/-- `addRestrictedProductSplit B T` as a measurable equivalence. -/]
noncomputable def restrictedProductSplitMeasurableEquiv :
    (Πʳ i, [G i, B i]) ≃ᵐ (Π i : T, G i) × Πʳ i : {i // i ∉ T}, [G i.val, B i.val] where
  toEquiv := (restrictedProductSplit B T).toEquiv
  measurable_toFun := measurable_restrictedProductSplit B T
  measurable_invFun := measurable_restrictedProductSplit_symm B T

/-- The underlying function of `restrictedProductSplitMeasurableEquiv B T` is
`restrictedProductSplit B T`. -/
@[to_additive (attr := simp) coe_addRestrictedProductSplitMeasurableEquiv
/-- The underlying function of `addRestrictedProductSplitMeasurableEquiv B T` is
`addRestrictedProductSplit B T`. -/]
theorem coe_restrictedProductSplitMeasurableEquiv :
    ⇑(restrictedProductSplitMeasurableEquiv B T) = restrictedProductSplit B T := by
  rfl

/-- The inverse of `restrictedProductSplitMeasurableEquiv B T` is the inverse of
`restrictedProductSplit B T`. -/
@[to_additive (attr := simp) coe_addRestrictedProductSplitMeasurableEquiv_symm
/-- The inverse of `addRestrictedProductSplitMeasurableEquiv B T` is the inverse of
`addRestrictedProductSplit B T`. -/]
theorem coe_restrictedProductSplitMeasurableEquiv_symm :
    ⇑(restrictedProductSplitMeasurableEquiv B T).symm = (restrictedProductSplit B T).symm := by
  rfl

end Split

end TauCeti
